{
    "word": "disillusionment",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "560c2284-e47f-3e17-8b52-fc035ffe4edf",
                "word": "disillusionment",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "abeb463e-9573-4ebc-8b68-28e4a4efcc0e",
                        "entry_id": "560c2284-e47f-3e17-8b52-fc035ffe4edf",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "disillusionments"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8d164442-f988-36e8-8da4-c0ac92ec0165",
                        "entry_id": "560c2284-e47f-3e17-8b52-fc035ffe4edf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A feeling of disappointment, akin to depression, arising from the realization that something is not what it was expected or believed to be, possibly accompanied by philosophical angst from having one's beliefs challenged."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4230dc75-bee9-4d0a-b09c-c67c8662f16d",
                                "sense_id": "8d164442-f988-36e8-8da4-c0ac92ec0165",
                                "text": "But till I am thirty, I know that my youth will triumph over everything- every disillusionment, every disgust with life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "edebc6c0-c736-4b11-a53e-aa54b34a0711",
                                "sense_id": "8d164442-f988-36e8-8da4-c0ac92ec0165",
                                "text": "I catch on your face the old sad smile / Of our ancient disillusionment, / When the ardent crowd tries to beguile / Your world-old soul to impassionment."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8f6c1f6-13af-4ad0-96bc-ae89801f4804",
                                "sense_id": "8d164442-f988-36e8-8da4-c0ac92ec0165",
                                "text": "They were self-conscious of their disillusionment and demoralization, and their spokesmen—the artists and journalists among them—publicized their cynicism so successfully that it came to be regarded as the mood of a whole decade."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a8e71a8-c046-4ca0-8eaa-806005ec6b71",
                                "sense_id": "8d164442-f988-36e8-8da4-c0ac92ec0165",
                                "text": "'Oh, this fair is nothing but a chaos of noise and beggars,' I thought in disillusionment. 'I wonder if Western scientists, patiently enlarging the realms of knowledge for the practical good of mankind, are not more pleasing to God than these idlers who profess religion but concentrate on alms.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "61eb7d56-964c-487b-8393-3608f1a728a2",
                                "sense_id": "8d164442-f988-36e8-8da4-c0ac92ec0165",
                                "text": "1953, Dwight D. Eisenhower, First State of the Union Address,\nOur country has come through a painful period of trial and disillusionment since the victory of 1945. We anticipated a world of peace and cooperation. The calculated pressures of aggressive communism have forced us, instead, to live in a world of turmoil."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9c7b7863-6895-3ea5-8309-bc7dbf9c4559",
                        "entry_id": "560c2284-e47f-3e17-8b52-fc035ffe4edf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of freeing from an illusion; the state of being freed therefrom."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bda5ea23-2b71-49f5-be0d-5dc408ade190",
                                "sense_id": "9c7b7863-6895-3ea5-8309-bc7dbf9c4559",
                                "text": "It is a very wholesome and regenerating change which a man undergoes when he \"comes to himself.\" […] It is a process of disillusionment. The scales have fallen away."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c8cace6c-c827-4e3a-ad1e-9d83deeac3bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "560c2284-e47f-3e17-8b52-fc035ffe4edf",
                        "source_sense_description": "feeling that arises from the discovery that something is not what it was anticipated to be",
                        "target_lang_word": "deziluze",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "71c854b2-115a-413f-9022-752b67f9556b",
                        "source_entry_id": "560c2284-e47f-3e17-8b52-fc035ffe4edf",
                        "source_sense_description": "feeling that arises from the discovery that something is not what it was anticipated to be",
                        "target_lang_word": "désillusion",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "désillusion",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3457151e-3b01-30f1-b649-8b1434ba2184",
                                        "entry_id": "f67911b4-459e-3bec-9ac7-fd8801c39347",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Perte d’une illusion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1b0b75e-f035-460a-8702-1d7b0c9b43cc",
                                                "sense_id": "3457151e-3b01-30f1-b649-8b1434ba2184",
                                                "text": "Jacques, dès les premiers jours, s’insurgea, voulant être lui-même et agir selon sa conscience qui, méticuleuse, lui prépara des mécomptes, des désillusions et une incertitude perpétuelle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6967d744-06de-4634-8e63-1429c6cfc562",
                                                "sense_id": "3457151e-3b01-30f1-b649-8b1434ba2184",
                                                "text": "Quelle n’est pas ma désillusion en découvrant sous chaque pied de vigne l’hydre de la question sociale."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f618daa-dcc0-400b-94b9-95274eb79636",
                                                "sense_id": "3457151e-3b01-30f1-b649-8b1434ba2184",
                                                "text": "Elle l’avait appelé Fidélio, et comme l’employé de mairie trouvait le nom difficile, elle lui donna deux francs qu’il accepta. Ce fut ma première désillusion à l’endroit de l’incorruptibilité des fonctionnaires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c469d685-a7ac-425c-9cc6-17ac5b8a6b08",
                                                "sense_id": "3457151e-3b01-30f1-b649-8b1434ba2184",
                                                "text": "Et elle prenait en pitié Elhamy en songeant aux désillusions qu’il avait dû subir depuis les semaines insouciantes de ses fiançailles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7aadea0-fc41-4dfb-bf76-9d6639cfa2f7",
                                                "sense_id": "3457151e-3b01-30f1-b649-8b1434ba2184",
                                                "text": "Filière en tension, extrêmement attrayante auprès des lycéens, la psychologie souffre d’une représentation biaisée, voire idéalisée, ce qui donne lieu parfois à de véritables désillusions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5113b87e-b1dc-413a-af2e-7d02dde68577",
                                                "sense_id": "3457151e-3b01-30f1-b649-8b1434ba2184",
                                                "text": "La France vit des heures de désillusion aussi profonde que celles qu’elle avait connues en mai 1940. La France pensait avoir le meilleur système de santé du monde, comme elle était convaincue d’avoir la meilleure armée du monde en 1940."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ce93f2bb-0ba5-47cf-aa19-9920ba4a8e22",
                        "source_entry_id": "560c2284-e47f-3e17-8b52-fc035ffe4edf",
                        "source_sense_description": "feeling that arises from the discovery that something is not what it was anticipated to be",
